run.rb: allow disabling KWIN_WAYLAND_NO_PERMISSION_CHECKS from the outside

run.rb hard-codes the permission-check bypass before exec'ing the nested
kwin_wayland. With checks disabled KWin never reads the client's
X-KDE-Wayland-Interfaces and so never marks a client as privileged for
xdg-activation token grants: on KWin < 6.5 a non-privileged client can only
obtain a token while it owns the active surface, which makes a packaged dock
application unable to activate its own Settings window after the user clicks
its context menu (test_set001 fails on debian-13 / ubuntu-25.04 / 25.10).

All clients that bind privileged interfaces in this harness
(inputsynth, appidlister) ship .desktop files declaring
X-KDE-Wayland-Interfaces, and Tier 3 runs krema from its installed distro
package (com.bhyoo.krema.desktop declares the interfaces too), so letting the
testsuite ask for real permission checks exercises the packaging contract.
Tier 2 runs krema from the build tree, which no desktop file can match, so
the default must stay enabled: entrypoint.sh exports
KWIN_WAYLAND_NO_PERMISSION_CHECKS=0 only for Tier 3 runs and run.rb now
honours a pre-set value.

--- a/run.rb
+++ b/run.rb
@@ -110,5 +110,5 @@
     ENV['QT_QPA_PLATFORM'] = 'wayland'
     ENV['KWIN_SCREENSHOT_NO_PERMISSION_CHECKS'] = '1'
-    ENV['KWIN_WAYLAND_NO_PERMISSION_CHECKS'] = '1'
+    ENV['KWIN_WAYLAND_NO_PERMISSION_CHECKS'] ||= '1'
     ENV['KWIN_PID'] = pid.to_s
     ENV['KWIN_XKB_DEFAULT_KEYMAP'] = 'true'
